codex
| id | file:line-ish | issue | severity | why-real |
|---|---|---:|---|---|
| F1 | `run_riscvdv_lockstep.py:430-459` | `watchdog_trap_waiver` can waive after an unverified DUT tail. | High | On watchdog, Spike is capped at `200_000` instructions while DUT can have far more commits. The function only checks `min(len(dut), len(spike))` prefix, then compares the last DUT trap to the last Spike exception without requiring that DUT trap to occur within the verified prefix or at the next unverified boundary. A real divergence/livelock after the matched prefix can be waived if the later trap tuple matches. |
| F2 | `run_riscvdv_lockstep.py:400-427` | `matched_nested_trap_waiver` accepts any later matching DUT trap, not the first unpaired event. | Medium | After confirming `dut[:len(spike)] == spike`, it scans all DUT trap entries with `idx >= expected_idx` and all Spike exceptions. That can waive a run where DUT diverges after Spike ends, executes extra/unverified commits, and later hits a trap matching some Spike exception. The predicate should be tied to the immediate unpaired trap/event, not any future matching trap. |
| F3 | `dv_farm.py:66-69`, `dv_farm.py:89-91`, `dv_farm.py:140-156` | Campaigns share `runs/seed_<n>` and status files are not cleared for reused campaign names. | Medium | Two farms, or a farm plus serial run, using overlapping seeds will `rmtree` the same work dir. Separately, rerunning `--campaign same_name` leaves old `status/seed_*.json` files and the rollup counts stale seeds not in the current run. Both can corrupt reported results without any DUT issue. |

No real bug found in `gen_core` install-once parallelization itself: for this `pyflow` path, generated asm/log/seed outputs are under each seed’s `--output`, and the installed target config is read-only while workers run.

No real bug found in the Grok-safe `dut[:_i+1]` terminal trim from the reviewed code. The TB exits on the terminal store before logging that store as a commit, so trimming to the first `write_tohost` commit does not appear to drop an otherwise comparable DUT commit.
